drm/apple: blend XRGB2101010 as premultiplied

XRGB2101010 maps to l10r, which has alpha, so its two X bits are read as
alpha. The premultiplied-over-black workaround for formats without alpha
lists XBGR2101010 instead, which appledrm neither advertises nor maps; a
client buffer scanned out directly with garbage X bits would turn partly
transparent. Treat XRGB2101010 like the other X formats.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/plane.c
@@ -232,6 +232,7 @@
 	 */
 	if (fmt->format == DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888 ||
 	    fmt->format == DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888 ||
+	    fmt->format == DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010 ||
 	    fmt->format == DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010)
 		is_premultiplied = true;
 
